# Build context is ./src/backend (see docker-compose.yml). Docker only reads the
# .dockerignore at the ROOT of the build context, so the repo-root .dockerignore was
# never applied and host bin/obj leaked into the image — `COPY . .` then overwrote the
# container's restore with Windows project.assets.json and `publish --no-restore` broke.
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules

